# Target C: leaf-fan sector run

Date: 2026-10-02.
Starting shared checkout: `539f5187b3cac9287f6b30cdf6b36aafb1763c5a`.
Starting research base: `75aac1464f80ca91256e96dc70ca0c865e0b3b0e`.
State version: `2026-09-14.audit.51`.
Mission: exact diameter-leaf fans, their inward spokes, and stopped rhombus trains.
Branch: `swarm/sol/leaf-fan-sector-20261002`.
Classification at initialization: unreviewed candidate. Level I and C-II remain open.

`fan-edge unique support -> fan trains end on actual defect incidences -> exact Q/x_B charge; a contradiction still requires an independent upper bound on that same currency or a finite source competitor.`

Canonical inputs actually used: Target C Sections 26/35 (fully visible contact core,
loaded extremality/degree and unloaded harmonicity), Sections 57/58 (full-support
normalization, full-source geometry), Section 61 (finite stopped-rhombus trains and
face-incidence currency), and Section 63 (distinguished outer-walk intervals).
Unpromoted dependencies to be audited before application: current-main leaf-fan
outer-walk reduction (`abdbe1f5`) and inward-spoke fork (`75aac146`).

Initial concrete attacks:

1. Prove that an inward third neighbor is strictly inside the triangle formed by the
   carrier and the two neighboring fan leaves, and hence is unloaded.
2. Test whether consecutive third spokes force nonquadrilateral faces; construct an
   exact positive-equilibrium rhombic collar if they do not.
3. Prove that a fan unit chord has a unique opposite supporting vertex (its carrier),
   then count the actual stopped-train endpoints without identifying source points
   with abstract train or response vertices.

No canonical theorem-state change or promotion is authorized by this report.

Durable results are in
`docs/reports/target_c_leaf_fan_stopped_train_and_collar_2026-10-02.md`.
The fan-count dependency is rederived from canonical Woodall and outer-walk
inputs; the inward triangle is proved directly. New candidates are the unique
opposite support, stopped-train charge `5Q >= h-3nu-3x_B`, rank-to-face
transport `s_Z <= 2f+3nu+x_B`, and common-train area surcharge
`E_4 >= Rg(g-1)/(8D)` under the stated small-width/full-crossing hypotheses.

The exact positive-equilibrium rhombic collar rejects a local spoke-to-non4
inference. Its missing carrier and four endpoint equations are recorded;
it is not a global-minimum or full-stress counterexample. Certificate:
`research/verify_target_c_leaf_fan_sector_2026_10_02.py`.

The next area attack was performed and does not close square-root fans:
`g=Theta(sqrt(D)), R=Theta(D)` costs only `Theta(D)`, consistent with the
linear full-source area budget when `Z_ext=O(D)`. The surviving obstruction
is the completed source's actual non4 train endpoints, not local rhombic
immunity or an unproved positive multiplier floor.
